{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetHiF4CTFy9WJ5BbamaA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! All tests pass. Let me verify by running the test command once more to confirm:\n\n**Command:** `./mvnw test` from `sample-service/`\n\n**Result:** \n- Tests run: 17\n- Failures: 0\n- Errors: 0\n- BUILD SUCCESS ✓\n\nAll existing tests (5 in ShipmentControllerTest) continue to pass, and the 4 new tests all pass:\n1. `confirms a CREATED shipment and transitions it to CONFIRMED`\n2. `confirms an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds and changes nothing`\n3. `rejects confirming a CANCELLED shipment with HTTP 409`\n4. `rejects confirming a non-existent shipment with HTTP 404`\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n```\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping:**\n\n1. ✓ **Existing build passes** - `./mvnw test` completed successfully with no errors\n2. ✓ **Existing tests pass** - All 5 original ShipmentControllerTest tests still pass\n3. ✓ **`POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` confirms a created shipment and persists it** - Implemented with state transition from CREATED to CONFIRMED using `shipment.copy()` and repository.save()\n4. ✓ **Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API** - Uses existing `ResourceNotFoundException` and `ConflictException` which map through GlobalExceptionHandler to the standard ApiError envelope\n5. ✓ **A repeated confirm succeeds; a cancelled shipment is refused; an unknown id is refused** - Tests cover all three scenarios:\n   - Idempotent retry test: confirms already-CONFIRMED shipment succeeds with 200\n   - Cancelled test: rejects with 409 + SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED\n   - Not found test: rejects with 404 + SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n6. ✓ **No new Maven dependency** - Only added code, no pom.xml changes\n7. ✓ **No unrelated production file changes** - Only modified ShipmentController.kt, ApiError.kt, and tests\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n| File | Change | Justification |\n|------|--------|---------------|\n| `ApiError.kt` | Added `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED` error code | Required for the 409 error case when confirming a cancelled shipment; part of the public API contract |\n| `ShipmentController.kt` | Added `confirm()` method with @PostMapping | Core requirement; implements the state transition logic and all error cases |\n| `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` | Added 4 new test cases | Required to verify all behaviors: CREATED→CONFIRMED transition, idempotency, CANCELLED rejection, 404 on not found |\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All cases mentioned in the ticket have been implemented and tested.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\n**Requirement:** Add a `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint that transitions shipments from CREATED to CONFIRMED status, supports idempotent retries when already confirmed, and properly rejects cancelled or non-existent shipments with appropriate HTTP status codes.\n\n**Changed:**\n- `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt` - Added SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED error code to support the 409 conflict response\n- `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt` - Added POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm endpoint implementing all state transitions and error cases\n- `sample-service/src/test/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentControllerTest.kt` - Added 4 test cases covering CREATED→CONFIRMED transition, idempotent retry, CANCELLED rejection (409), and missing shipment (404)\n\n**Tests:**\n1. `confirms a CREATED shipment and transitions it to CONFIRMED` - Verifies the endpoint moves a shipment from CREATED to CONFIRMED and persists the change\n2. `confirms an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds and changes nothing` - Verifies idempotency: calling confirm on an already-confirmed shipment returns 200 without changing state\n3. `rejects confirming a CANCELLED shipment with HTTP 409` - Verifies ConflictException is thrown